    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27173" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διολισθάνω</span></b>  (in <i><span class="en">
			Pl.
			<u>Ly.</u>
			216d
		</span></i> codd. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-αίνω,</span> cf. <i><span class="en">
			Luc.
			<u>Cont.</u>
			1
		</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
			Lib.
			<u>Or.</u>
			11.225
		</span></i>), 
			Ion.
		
		aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ωλίσθησα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Art.</u>
					63
				</span></i>
			: aor. 2
			inf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διολισθεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					434
				</span></i>
			:—<i>slip through,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ τοὺς δακτύλους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Art.</u>
					40
				</span></i>
			; of a bone put out, ib.<i><span class="en">
				63
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. τοὺς χρήστας</span>
			<i>to give</i> them <i>the slip,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
			</span></i> l. c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. καὶ διαδύεται ἡμᾶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
				</span></i>
			 l. c.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽ ἄκρων δ.
			κυμάτων,</span> of a ship, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Dom.</u>
				12
			</span></i>: abs., <i>slip away,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Anach.</u>
				28
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				29
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. τὴν γλῶσσαν</span>
			<i>slipping</i> with his tongue, of one drunken, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Vit.Auct.</u>
				12
			</span></i>.</div>
